  "visual_review": "All three native 17-frame videos inspected at f0/f4/f8/f12/f16 against source. Gain 0.5 rapidly fades to near invisibility; gain 1.0 fades late; gain 1.5 keeps the dancer clearer and more stable. Yet at gain 1.5 the right arm/wrist and overall action remain nearly fixed while source changes substantially. The persistent pose mismatch means the stronger control is a visual-clarity improvement, not a holistic Stage3 pass.",
  "caveat": "Joint MAE depends on matched detectable frames; contrast is an uncalibrated image proxy and can miss structural failure. No universal quality threshold or best-angle claim.",
  "conclusion": "The camera-encoder gain controls the fade/clarity tradeoff in this case. Uniform gain alone does not restore action continuation; next Stage3 work must preserve motion while retaining target-view detail.",
